-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 17 14:00:00 UTC 2026 - Lyra OS Release <rodrigo@lyraos.com.br>

- Ship /etc/pki/tls/certs/ca-bundle.crt as a link to the openSUSE CA
  bundle (/etc/ssl/ca-bundle.pem) and require ca-certificates. The core
  only looks for the Red Hat path to validate the manufacturer's
  download server; without it, installing the bank client files
  aborted and banks kept asking for the security module (warsaw#18).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 17 13:00:00 UTC 2026 - Lyra OS Release <rodrigo@lyraos.com.br>

- %check also compares the packaged file list with
  warsaw-files.sha256: a new vendor file outside the manifest now
  fails the build instead of shipping without a hash check (warsaw#3).
- Erase and upgrade stop the helpers by executable
  (/proc/<pid>/exe under /usr/local/bin/warsaw/) instead of a pkill -f
  command-line pattern, so a helper started with another argv[0] no
  longer survives (warsaw#2).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Nov 15 21:30:00 UTC 2026 - Lyra OS Release <rodrigo@lyraos.com.br>

- Add a polkit rule that lets the active local session start and
  stop only warsaw.service, without a password. The Vega bank web
  apps start the service when they open and stop it when they close
  (vega#210). Enable, disable, mask and other units still need the
  administrator password.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Nov 15 18:45:00 UTC 2026 - Lyra OS Release <rodrigo@lyraos.com.br>

- Own /usr/local/etc again: no openSUSE package owns it and the OBS
  filelist check rejects unowned directories. Filter rpmlint's
  standard-dir-owned-by-package for that directory.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Nov 15 20:00:00 UTC 2026 - Lyra OS Release <rodrigo@lyraos.com.br>

- Use the openSUSE %service_add_pre, %service_add_post,
  %service_del_preun and %service_del_postun macros.
- Stop owning /usr/local/etc, which belongs to the standard hierarchy.
- Rewrite warsaw-rpmlintrc for rpmlint 2: drop the filters that matched
  nothing and filter, with a documented reason, only the errors that
  come from the unmodified vendor payload (/usr/local layout, init
  script, executable stack in wsbrmu.so, setuid without setgroups in
  core).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Nov 15 18:40:00 UTC 2026 - Lyra OS Release <rodrigo@lyraos.com.br>

- Add Epoch: 1 so the package supersedes the vendor 2.21.4-3: OBS
  rewrites Release to lp161.N.M, which sorts below the vendor "3".
  Use Release: 0, as OBS replaces it anyway.
- Detect the vendor RPM in %pre by its missing Epoch instead of the
  release string.
- List each %license file on its own line; rpm rejected two absolute
  paths on one line.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Nov 15 16:00:00 UTC 2026 - Lyra OS Release <rodrigo@lyraos.com.br>

- Mark only gas.dbd as %config(noreplace), as the vendor RPM does;
  config.cfgc, features.datc and uninstall.dat now follow each upgrade
  (gh#lyra-os-linux/warsaw#7).
- Disable warsaw.service at boot when replacing the vendor RPM, which
  enables it in its %post (gh#lyra-os-linux/warsaw#8).
- Stop warsaw.service and its helpers in %pre before replacing files on
  upgrade, and start it again in %posttrans only if it was running
  (gh#lyra-os-linux/warsaw#9).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 15:04:10 UTC 2026 - Lyra OS Release <rodrigo@lyraos.com.br>

- Package the official Warsaw 2.21.4-3 x86_64 RPM for the signed Lyra
  repositories without recompiling or modifying its payload. Use
  Release 3.lyra1 so it supersedes the unsigned vendor RPM of the same
  version if one is already installed.
- Replace the obsolete procps-ng requirement with procps.
- Keep warsaw.service disabled on install, ship a preset that prevents
  systemd from enabling it, and stop/disable it on erase.
- Verify every packaged file against the pinned upstream SHA-256 list.

